      "contactEmail": "privacy@postqron.com",
      "content": "# Postqron Cookie Policy\n\n## 1. Who issues this policy\n\nThis Cookie Policy is issued by Apdsoftware di Carlo Zuffetti (Via C. Colombo 15, 24047 Treviglio (BG), Italy, VAT number 03835250162, REA (company registration number) BG 431224), trading as APDSoftware, operator of the Postqron social-media-scheduling service (\"Postqron\", \"we\", \"us\"; entity information verified via a public source: https://mailronix.com/terms, consulted 2026-07-25), reachable at privacy@postqron.com and https://apdsoftware.it.\n\n## 2. What this policy covers\n\nThis policy explains how cookies, browser local storage, and similar technologies are used on postqron.com and within the Postqron application. Your choices about non-essential technologies are collected through a consent mechanism that organizes technologies into four categories: **necessary**, **preferences**, **analytics**, and **marketing**. Only the **necessary** category is active before you make any choice. The other three categories require your explicit opt-in, and nothing classified under them loads or runs until you have given consent.\n\n## 3. Cookie inventory\n\nThe table below lists every cookie, local storage item, and third-party script currently in use by Postqron. This inventory is exhaustive as of the version stated above.\n\n| Name | Set by | Category | Purpose | Duration | First/third-party |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `__Host-postqron_session` | Postqron backend (authentication) | necessary | Authenticates the logged-in session | Session-length, tied to the session's expiry | First-party |\n| `__Host-postqron_cookie_subject` | Postqron backend (cookie-consent service) | necessary | Anonymous pseudonymous identifier used to record and apply your cookie choice before you are logged in | 183 days (6 months) | First-party |\n| `postqron_locale` | Postqron frontend | necessary (functional) | Remembers your selected interface language; contains no personal data | 365 days | First-party |\n| `postqron.cookie-choice` (browser local storage, not a cookie) | Postqron frontend | necessary (functional) | Client-side cache of the cookie choice already confirmed with our server | Until cleared or updated by a new choice | First-party, local storage only, not sent to any server |\n| Paddle checkout script (`https://cdn.paddle.com/paddle/v2/paddle.js`) and any cookies it sets | Paddle | Not classified by Postqron — governed entirely by Paddle | Loaded only on the billing/checkout page to process payment | Governed by Paddle, not set or controlled by Postqron | Third-party, scoped strictly to the checkout flow |\n\n## 4. No analytics, preferences, or marketing trackers today\n\nAs of this version, Postqron does not set or load any cookie, pixel, SDK, or script under the **preferences**, **analytics**, or **marketing** categories. These categories exist within the consent mechanism for potential future use, are strictly opt-in, and currently have zero registered trackers. Nothing is tracked, measured, or targeted under them today. If this changes, the inventory in Section 3 will be updated and users will be asked for a fresh consent choice before any new non-essential technology is loaded.\n\n## 5. Your choices\n\nOn your first visit, no optional technology loads before you make a choice. The consent banner presents \"Accept all\", \"Reject all\", and \"Customize\" with equal visual prominence, and no options are pre-ticked in your favor. A recorded choice is stored for a maximum of 6 months. You may review or change your choice at any time using the \"Review your cookie choices\" link available in the site footer or your account area; revoking consent takes no more steps than granting it. Withdrawing consent immediately stops any new reads or writes of non-necessary technologies, and any cookies you can access under those categories are removed.\n\n## 6. Contact\n\nIf you have questions about this Cookie Policy, please contact us at privacy@postqron.com.",
